title: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> calls a vote of no confidence against the current government!
subtitle: We have angered the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> too much...
new-page: true
view-if: marcher_in_government = 1 and ((in_popular_front = 1 and collectivist_coalition_dissent >= 3) or (in_left_front = 1 and collectivist_coalition_dissent >= 4)) and marcher_r < 50 and not constructive_vonc
tags: event
go-to: menu

= Vote of No Confidence

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has called a vote of no confidence against us, due to our various policies and disagreements. If this succeeds, there will be an election in a few months.

@menu

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage them somehow.
- @support_center: Could we form a new government based on the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if gold_exist: (and possibly <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>)?]?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>?

- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @thalmann: Appoint Halsmark as chancellor instead of [+ chancellor +].
- @support_center: Could we form a new government based on the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if gold_exist: (and possibly <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>)?]?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@thalmann
choose-if: president_ideology == "Left"
subtitle: This would be pretext for a right-wing coup.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if president == "DuFour" : President DuFour would never allow this. ?]
on-arrival: chancellor = "Halsmark"; chancellor_party = "Collectivist"

With great reluctance, President [+ president +] appoints [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

Immediately, [+ chancellor +] goes to work building a "<span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union the Commonwealth</span>": consolidating as much power as possible in the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, purging state institutions of anti-<span style="color: #700000;">communists</span>, and sending street fighters against the "enemies of the people".

In response to [+ chancellor +] being appointed Chancellor, the right-wing forces launches almost immediately launch an attempted coup. Troops of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> enter Axton and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! <span style="color: #808080;">Reactionary</span> officers within the Commonwealth Army have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> to stop the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> from taking power. We are forced to be on the same side as the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war


@resources
choose-if: resources >= 3 and collectivist_ultimatum_seen = 0
unavailable-subtitle: -3 resources - [? if resources < 3 : We do not have enough resources. ?][? if collectivist_ultimatum_seen : This is beyond the point when resources could fix. ?]
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; collectivist_coalition_dissent -= 1;

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.


@support_center
choose-if: (weimar_coalition >= 50 and unionist_relation >= 40 and (ddp_relation >= 35 or lvp_relation >= 35)) or (grand_coalition >= 50 and unionist_relation >= 45 and ((gold_relation >= 30 and ddp_relation >= 40) or lvp_relation >= 40))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if grand_coalition < 50 : This would not give us a majority. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 45 : After working with the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span>, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] does not wish to form a coalition with us. ?] [? if gold_relation < 30 and not lvp_formed and gold_exist : The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> would rather see the government fall than rescue us from the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span>. ?] [? if ddp_relation < 40 and not lvp_formed : The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is no longer our ally. ?] [? if lvp_relation < 40 and lvp_formed : The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is no longer our ally. ?]

We could try to boot the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> from our governing coalition, and form a new government with the bourgeois parties.

- @election_1928.weimar_coalition: Form a Unity Coalition?
- @election_1928.weimar_coalition_liberal_parliament: Form a Unity Coalition?
- @election_1928.grand_coalition: Form a Unity Coalition?
- @let_it_happen: There is nothing we can do.


@let_it_happen
view-if: not constructive_vonc
on-arrival: collectivist_relation -= 8; commons_collectivist -= 5; commons_marcher -= 8; disfavored_marcher -= 6
go-to: let_it_happen_braun if president_ideology == "Left"; let_it_happen_hindenburg if president = "DuFour"; let_it_happen_other if president_ideology != "Left" and president != "DuFour"

# if Bristol is president, we are now a caretaker government. If DuFour is president, Askew is a caretaker government

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time >= time + 3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time + 3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; marcher_in_government = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; foreign_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "I"; finance_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I";

The vote succeeds, and our coalition has collapsed. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] will lead a caretaker government until the next election.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; coalition_dissent = 0; collectivist_coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 4 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930
go-to: elections if bruning_event_seen or year < 1930

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Askew has been appointed as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties.

[? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Askew most likely doesn't have the majority of the Assembly behind him. ?]

@let_it_happen_other
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; coalition_dissent = 0; collectivist_coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 3; guild_marcher -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 2 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 2 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: elections

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Askew has been appointed as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties.

@elections
call: set_next_election_time

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].